Principles of Quantum Computing and Cryptography

1. Fundamentals of Qubits and Superposition

Unlike classical bits which exist deterministically as 0 or 1, quantum bits (qubits) exist in a superposition of states represented mathematically as |psi> = alpha|0> + beta|1>, where |alpha|^2 + |beta|^2 = 1. This property allows quantum computers to evaluate vast combinatorial solution spaces simultane